# The parent's constructor runs first, so its keys come first: one allocation lists x ahead of m, and asks no table of key orders. f1 = run
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK-NOT: HasKeyOrder
# CHECK: = NewObject -, {{*}} layout=L1 fields=[1, 0]
# CHECK-NOT: HasKeyOrder
# RUN(FIELDS): link fields mechanisms=all
# FIELDS: field L1.0 "m"
# FIELDS: field L1.1 "x"
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell
# ANSWERS: x,m
